{"title":"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2,_Barycentric_(Modified_by_Evan_Chen)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2, Barycentric (Modified by Evan Chen)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Cartesian)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Cartesian)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Complex)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Complex)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point in the plane of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> a line passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> be the points where the reflections of lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f988caff51f7fc88ad40d1d25022c52ffd8f976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e049532148caaf1c48e37658b548a6255c8d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> intersect lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">sine law</a> on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebb5cd774243a8552ce9ff3d3c1f769e837023ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&#39;P$\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86fce1df80a4efae66578a78af93fd881bf8292a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AB&#39;}{\\sin \\angle APB&#39;} = \\frac{AP}{\\sin \\angle AB&#39;P},\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"38\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/55210cdd21ff6980e44a1625c7f6be6e69919d14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB&#39; = AP \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle APB&#39;}{\\sin \\angle AB&#39;P}.\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/14470c134908465d5b19f90782af1e3c0d315654.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; import geometry;  unitsize(0.5 cm);  pair[] A, B, C; pair P, R;  A[0] = (2,12); B[0] = (0,0); C[0] = (14,0); P = (4,5); R = 5*dir(70); A[1] = extension(B[0],C[0],P,reflect(P + R,P - R)*(A[0])); B[1] = extension(C[0],A[0],P,reflect(P + R,P - R)*(B[0])); C[1] = extension(A[0],B[0],P,reflect(P + R,P - R)*(C[0]));  draw((P - R)--(P + R),red); draw(A[1]--B[1]--C[1]--cycle,blue); draw(A[0]--B[0]--C[0]--cycle); draw(A[0]--P); draw(B[0]--P); draw(C[0]--P); draw(P--A[1]); draw(P--B[1]); draw(P--C[1]); draw(A[1]--B[0]); draw(A[1]--B[0]);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A[0], N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B[0], S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C[0], SE); dot(&quot;$A&#39;$&quot;, A[1], SW); dot(&quot;$B&#39;$&quot;, B[1], NE); dot(&quot;$C&#39;$&quot;, C[1], W); dot(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, SE); label(&quot;$\\gamma$&quot;, P + R, N); [/asy]\" width=\"462\" height=\"328\" />\n</p><p>Similarly,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259479610aded2719a8a1fada1c3ea1ec2913445.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} B&#39;C &amp;= CP \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle CPB&#39;}{\\sin \\angle CB&#39;P}, \\\\ CA&#39; &amp;= CP \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle CPA&#39;}{\\sin \\angle CA&#39;P}, \\\\ A&#39;B &amp;= BP \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle BPA&#39;}{\\sin \\angle BA&#39;P}, \\\\ BC&#39; &amp;= BP \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle BPC&#39;}{\\sin \\angle BC&#39;P}, \\\\ C&#39;A &amp;= AP \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle APC&#39;}{\\sin \\angle AC&#39;P}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"193\" height=\"215\" />\nHence,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf22002a6564dbee3cdd65952fa0efada6aa0c23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} &amp;\\frac{AB&#39;}{B&#39;C} \\cdot \\frac{CA&#39;}{A&#39;B} \\cdot \\frac{BC&#39;}{C&#39;A} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sin \\angle APB&#39;}{\\sin \\angle AB&#39;P} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle CB&#39;P}{\\sin \\angle CPB&#39;} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle CPA&#39;}{\\sin \\angle CA&#39;P} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle BA&#39;P}{\\sin \\angle BPA&#39;} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle BPC&#39;}{\\sin \\angle BC&#39;P} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\angle AC&#39;P}{\\sin \\angle APC&#39;}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"628\" height=\"82\" />\n</p><p>Since angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1d86c3d73eaf7c3806f9c79698da7412eb1a7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AB&#39;P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/3991d28cad20ecd2f37e38edc31dab34925fe963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CB&#39;P$\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> are supplementary or equal, depending on the position of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b5697930dcc2a9ab38e715adac60903f4e59535.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin \\angle AB&#39;P = \\sin \\angle CB&#39;P.\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"14\" />\nSimilarly,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9310e589fd24b2a06aa4ce93319ca417db05a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sin \\angle CA&#39;P &amp;= \\sin \\angle BA&#39;P, \\\\ \\sin \\angle BC&#39;P &amp;= \\sin \\angle AC&#39;P. \\end{align*}\" width=\"197\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>By the reflective property, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/7/f07e09f24ffb6a0000a4b4ec655c1db87433b063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB&#39;$\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e150593d72afdbf4bc319b2654f6d6cad19f4123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BPA&#39;$\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> are supplementary or equal, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c7f47b5b1d4059649a57746c98fd5eb66013542.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin \\angle APB&#39; = \\sin \\angle BPA&#39;.\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"14\" />\nSimilarly,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc05510b6e9e30497545730655188885aa290d2c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sin \\angle CPA&#39; &amp;= \\sin \\angle APC&#39;, \\\\ \\sin \\angle BPC&#39; &amp;= \\sin \\angle CPB&#39;. \\end{align*}\" width=\"199\" height=\"40\" />\nTherefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a98a03ba637313347050b9f9b77942348d35b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AB&#39;}{B&#39;C} \\cdot \\frac{CA&#39;}{A&#39;B} \\cdot \\frac{BC&#39;}{C&#39;A} = 1,\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"38\" />\nso by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Menelaus%27_Theorem\" title=\"Menelaus&#39; Theorem\">Menelaus's theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.2C_Barycentric_.28Modified_by_Evan_Chen.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2,_Barycentric_(Modified_by_Evan_Chen)\">Solution 2, Barycentric (Modified by Evan Chen)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2, Barycentric (Modified by Evan Chen)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will perform barycentric coordinates on the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/0271c07d962987f77a7e70ca22952b839348768c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PCC&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d6fdfb6ac7625165f91ab303536e0da4405765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=(1,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2cedb8b5ff7c95ae62de6266d0f37f318c03724e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;=(0,1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/0601dfe585e5f1db64ff77ab451365145c24c9b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=(0,0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />. Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c45e1158bbae891818b1b101ca1fdf5d0d1052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = CC&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9013c1167e062f0fbe9e4a2c2126298613fec7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = CP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/6/fa6b1846ab616b6da556d3bb3f3cf380ad146912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = C&#39;P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> as usual. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear, we will define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/3479987755e7d4f5393c34f4d54bea83b30fd280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (p : k : q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/3564809b570eef34b1d9464f3a2326a04dc86b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (p : \\ell : q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Claim: Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> is the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/96741f9a8943bcd215a1eb4148dc9864674c286b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APA&#39;$\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/769ff7f1c5a79261def290670f60b825f8dc9253.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BPB&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e675c2dba16f629e0f6fec097d73b9eb46807d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CPC&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />. \nThis is proved by observing that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a78eb3b5ceedce75cbdc76a5c2040f2804c30d83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> is the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />, etc.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the intersection of the isogonal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4a1d658cc836e09898f34aa1757eae5c5cedaf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle P$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />\nwith the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />; that is,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/8/b180b93312f2aaca7997eefd1f7efb54c765516a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B&#39; = \\left( \\frac pk \\frac{b^2}{\\ell}: \\frac{b^2}{\\ell} : \\frac{c^2}{q} \\right).\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"43\" />\nAnalogously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> is the intersection of the isogonal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4a1d658cc836e09898f34aa1757eae5c5cedaf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle P$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />\nwith the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />; that is,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/127394291ca0dd453c7064238c6d37f8d3917f21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A&#39; = \\left( \\frac{p}{\\ell} \\frac{b^2}{k} : \\frac{b^2}{k} : \\frac{c^2}{q} \\right).\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"43\" />\nThe ratio of the first to third coordinate in these two points\nis both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1bec4f61954b5d32bda0c6751698d53d479b0a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2pq : c^2k\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, so it follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b798193cb94562989018728e1151587c618655b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear.\n</p><p>~peppapig_\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Cartesian.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Cartesian)\">Solution 3 (Cartesian)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Cartesian)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will use Cartesian coordinates. Without loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc5a6a2ca3dea63807ed8f4a503e7bb69eafbfa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = (0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> be the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/7/d97a72a3c89b764d2a8774f36b207fdc3e168c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (x_1,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f469bb15404f061363981f6e82dc9e56d9f6b97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (x_2,y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/6/ef63d15fd42e3566d2d0bdec693b393c11a2eed8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (x_3,y_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> is the intersection of the lines\n\\begin{align*}\ny &amp;= -\\frac{y_1}{x_1}x \\\\\ny - y_2 &amp;= \\frac{y_2 - y_3}{x_2 - x_3}(x - x_2).\n\\end{align*}\nSolving the system of equations, we see it is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7b6f8ba889d23b1c97d95b60fc4a1064bc250a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{x_1(x_2y_3 - y_2x_3)}{x_1y_2 + y_1x_2 - x_1y_3 - x_3y_1},\\frac{y_1(y_2x_3 - x_2y_3)}{x_1y_2 + y_1x_2 - x_1y_3 - x_3y_1}\\right).\\]\" width=\"452\" height=\"43\" />\nTo check collinearity, we need the determinant of the matrix\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89b5fb9e61b4f46214bfa9257a1e528ad2e5780.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{bmatrix} x_1(x_2y_3 - y_2x_3) &amp; y_1(y_2x_3 - x_2y_3) &amp; x_1y_2 + y_1x_2 - x_1y_3 - x_3y_1 \\\\ x_2(x_3y_1 - y_3x_1) &amp; y_2(y_3x_1 - x_3y_1) &amp; x_2y_3 + y_2x_3 - x_2y_1 - x_1y_2 \\\\ x_3(x_1y_2 - y_1x_2) &amp; y_3(y_1x_2 - x_1y_2) &amp; x_3y_1 + y_3x_1 - x_3y_2 - x_2y_3 \\end{bmatrix}\\]\" width=\"493\" height=\"64\" />\nto be zero, which is true because the columns sum to zero.\n</p><p>~knowingant\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Complex.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Complex)\">Solution 4 (Complex)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Complex)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We establish a complex plane with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d3954d6d1ba0896ad0277fcb976ff6f2c981c843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and the equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b269f0e575a11161ac15b38e58149a1254d90310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Im}(z)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> (the real axis). Let the lowercase letter of each point denote its complex coordinate. Thus, we have the equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />:\n\\begin{gather*}\n\\frac{z}{\\overline z}=\\frac{\\overline a}{a}\\\\\n\\frac{b-z}{\\overline b-\\overline z}=\\frac{c-z}{\\overline c-\\overline z}\n\\end{gather*}\nSolving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f138b52163f31dc2dc5a4514c012d6edd5c5f2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;=\\frac{\\overline{a}(\\overline{b}c-b\\overline{c})}{\\overline{a}(\\overline{b}-\\overline{c})-a(b-c)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"190\" height=\"49\" />. Using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b491e615fdcd613b8f5feed9b3cc0dc286e15c05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z-\\overline{z}=2i\\cdot \\operatorname{Im}(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />, this simplifies to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/5051df17673599ccc1a68ddb397dbbf95d662dde.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a&#39;=\\frac{\\overline{a}\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline{b}c)}{\\operatorname{Im}\\bigl(\\overline{a}(\\overline{b}-\\overline{c})\\bigr)}\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"47\" />\nBy symmetry,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa64e348eb4dd281fd310577f8df1dde36d21d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b&#39;=\\frac{\\overline{b}\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline{c}a)}{\\operatorname{Im}\\bigl(\\overline{b}(\\overline{c}-\\overline{a})\\bigr)},\\quad c&#39;=\\frac{\\overline{c}\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline{a}b)}{\\operatorname{Im}\\bigl(\\overline{c}(\\overline{a}-\\overline{b})\\bigr)}\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"47\" />\nWe are interested whether the collinear determinant satisfies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10c79d7af452b7dd8e341a47734bbf38e59a0993.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{vmatrix} 1 &amp; a&#39; &amp; \\overline{a&#39;} \\\\ 1 &amp; b&#39; &amp; \\overline{b&#39;} \\\\ 1 &amp; c&#39; &amp; \\overline{c&#39;} \\end{vmatrix}=0\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"65\" />\nLet \n\\begin{gather*}\np_{bc}=\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline b c),\\quad q_{ca}=\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline c a), \\quad r_{ab}=\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline a b)\\\\\np_a=\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline a(\\overline b-\\overline c)),\\quad q_b=\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline b(\\overline c-\\overline a)),\\quad r_c=\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline c(\\overline a-\\overline b))\n\\end{gather*} \nWe proceed by solving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314a43c421e36611e21dfbdb760655dffdb6d0f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{vmatrix} 1 &amp; \\overline a\\cdot\\frac{p_{bc}}{p_a} &amp; a\\cdot\\frac{p_{bc}}{p_a} \\\\ 1 &amp; \\overline b\\cdot\\frac{q_{ca}}{q_b} &amp; b\\cdot\\frac{q_{ca}}{q_b} \\\\ 1 &amp; \\overline c\\cdot\\frac{r_{ab}}{r_c} &amp; c\\cdot\\frac{r_{ab}}{r_c} \\end{vmatrix}.\\]\" width=\"148\" height=\"68\" />\n</p><p>Evaluating the determinant yields\n\\begin{align*}\n&amp;\\frac{p_{bc}}{p_a}\\cdot\\frac{q_{ca}}{q_b}(\\overline a b-a\\overline b)+\\frac{q_{ca}}{q_b}\\cdot\\frac{r_{ab}}{r_c}(\\overline b c-b\\overline c)-\\frac{r_{ab}}{r_c}\\cdot\\frac{p_{bc}}{p_a}(\\overline a c-a\\overline c)=0\\iff\\\\\n&amp;\\frac{p_{bc}}{p_a}\\cdot\\frac{q_{ca}}{q_b}\\cdot \\operatorname{Im}(\\overline a b)+\\frac{q_{ca}}{q_b}\\cdot\\frac{r_{ab}}{r_c}\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline b c)-\\frac{r_{ab}}{r_c}\\cdot\\frac{p_{bc}}{p_a}\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline a c)=0\\\\\n\\end{align*}\nBut <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/c/93cdc8beb6a9b59260c42c6c2b66fc7c3eb92bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline a c)=\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline c a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />, continuing simplifying:\n\\begin{align*} \n&amp;\\quad\\,\\,\\frac{p_{bc}}{p_a}\\cdot\\frac{q_{ca}}{q_b}\\cdot \\operatorname{Im}(\\overline a b)+\\frac{q_{ca}}{q_b}\\cdot\\frac{r_{ab}}{r_c}\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline b c)+\\frac{r_{ab}}{r_c}\\cdot \\frac{p_{bc}}{p_a}\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline c a)\\\\\n&amp;=p_{bc}\\cdot q_{ca}\\cdot r_{ab}\\left(\\frac{1}{p_a\\cdot q_b}+\\frac{1}{q_b\\cdot r_c}+\\frac{1}{r_c\\cdot p_a}\\right)\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{p_{bc}}{p_a}\\cdot\\frac{q_{ca}}{q_b}\\cdot \\frac{r_{ab}}{r_c}(p_a+q_b+r_c)\n\\end{align*}\nWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e00e4814763871a1acbf2bd3edc4710612acee1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline a(\\overline b-\\overline c))+\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline b(\\overline c-\\overline a))+\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline c(\\overline a-\\overline b))=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"372\" height=\"23\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>Note: We assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/6448f1ce66a69fa268c1aa8b8b6e46785a880f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_a\\cdot q_b\\cdot r_c\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />, since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c0ddf763c78938b36465641354a885f2756a559.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\operatorname{Im}(\\overline a(\\overline b-\\overline c))=0\\iff \\overline a(\\overline b-\\overline c)\\in\\mathbb{R}\\iff a(b-c)\\in\\mathbb{R}\\]\" width=\"430\" height=\"20\" />\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1e51ef5511c6d27c703b84edc8ff93ffbc3717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;$\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> is collinear with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5f448ea690deaa5999f3ef4417217e30c0630f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e0ac2ed7286cf4c59ff35696cc2daaf73594f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arg{a&#39;}=\\arg{\\overline a}=-\\arg{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"19\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/7/e67272f282f20e606837bd314f2d8f2d20088424.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arg{\\frac{1}{b-c}}=-\\arg{b-c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"180\" height=\"40\" />. It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0b14528f0c81d2cd699f16d2fde4db546a5f29f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a&#39;}{b-c}\\in\\mathbb{R}\\]\" width=\"74\" height=\"38\" />\nThe geometric interpretation of the above statement is that the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> across <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66981fa3920210c6ad8dbe5e968783d5dd7520c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, which does not result in an intersection point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> in an Euclidean plane. The same logic applies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c50362544f0c11fc5d99f1b1b04ab5a4399703d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/7/aa7620a597a75f93da094b677121f6080020f2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\">USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://geometry.ru/articles/DFdemystified.pdf\">Generalization of Droz-Farny line theorem</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO\" title=\"2012 USAMO\">2012 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><